# A loop of mandatory actions with a mandatory draw in it is no draw: the library runs out, and the player who draws from
# it empty loses (CR 104.4b, 704.5b). Bot2 Entombs its own Worldgorger Dragon on turn 2 and casts Robot Domination on turn
# 8 ("Whenever one or more creature cards are put into your graveyard from anywhere, you draw a card, lose 1 life, and put a
# plan counter on this enchantment"), with one card left in its library. On turn 9 Bot1 casts Necromancy on the Dragon, the
# only creature card in a graveyard, and the loop of the Necromancy draw scenario begins: the Dragon, Bot1's, exiles
# Necromancy and Bot1's Swamps; Necromancy's leaves ability sacrifices it, and it goes to its owner's graveyard, Bot2's
# (CR 404.1); its leaves ability returns them, and Necromancy's enters ability targets it again, its only choice. Each time
# the Dragon goes to Bot2's graveyard, Robot Domination's ability, Bot2's alone, makes Bot2 draw, lose 1 life and put a
# plan counter on it. The first time Bot2 draws its last card (19 life, one plan counter); the second time it draws from an
# empty library (18 life, two counters - the third, which would sacrifice it, never comes), and loses the game as the
# state-based actions are next checked (CR 704.5b). Bot1 wins. Each round came back to the board it left, but with Bot2's
# library a card shorter, and then with Bot2 having drawn from an empty library: never the same position twice.

